        <definition>constexpr uint32_t SimGateway::CDC_STALL_MS</definition>
        <argsstring></argsstring>
        <name>CDC_STALL_MS</name>
        <qualifiedname>SimGateway::CDC_STALL_MS</qualifiedname>
        <initializer>= 1000</initializer>
        <briefdescription>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>The CDC IN endpoint counts as stalled after this long with DTR held, bytes pending and nothing drained. The host OS keeps polling an open port into its own buffer even when the application is not reading, so a FIFO that stays full this long means the host&apos;s USB stack stopped polling — a configured-but-dead link that <computeroutput>mounted()</computeroutput> alone cannot see. </para>
        </detaileddescription>
