      <memberdef kind="function" id="namespaceSimGateway_1afa7f75ce54b436f48617b235a1ff2304" prot="public" static="no" const="no" explicit="no" inline="no" virt="non-virtual">
        <type>const <ref refid="structOpenSkyhawk_1_1CalBlob" kindref="compound">OpenSkyhawk::CalBlob</ref> &amp;</type>
        <definition>const OpenSkyhawk::CalBlob &amp; SimGateway::calibration</definition>
        <argsstring>()</argsstring>
        <name>calibration</name>
        <qualifiedname>SimGateway::calibration</qualifiedname>
        <briefdescription>
<para>The calibration currently applied to dispatched axis values. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para><simplesect kind="return"><para>The in-RAM blob, loaded by <ref refid="namespaceSimGateway_1aa708bae3840992ba113450b98dc0dc68" kindref="member">setup()</ref> from flash.</para>
</simplesect>
Every axis reads as uncalibrated until <ref refid="namespaceSimGateway_1aa708bae3840992ba113450b98dc0dc68" kindref="member">setup()</ref> loads a valid blob, so this is safe to call at any time. Use <ref refid="namespaceOpenSkyhawk_1a7c35dca075618dc50bf80ed5c4a760e2" kindref="member">OpenSkyhawk::axisCalValid()</ref> on an element to ask whether that particular axis is calibrated. </para>
        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
        </inbodydescription>
        <location file="Firmware/Libraries/SimGateway/SimGateway.cpp" line="1208" column="28" bodyfile="Firmware/Libraries/SimGateway/SimGateway.cpp" bodystart="1208" bodyend="1208" declfile="Firmware/Libraries/SimGateway/SimGateway.h" declline="281" declcolumn="28"/>
