      <memberdef kind="function" id="namespaceSimGateway_1aa8f7b2f81634cf26fff1d4d03b3ec70b" prot="public" static="no" const="no" explicit="no" inline="no" virt="non-virtual">
        <type>void</type>
        <definition>void SimGateway::loop</definition>
        <argsstring>()</argsstring>
        <name>loop</name>
        <qualifiedname>SimGateway::loop</qualifiedname>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Relay bytes and dispatch HID frames. Call once per <ref refid="namespaceSimGateway_1aa8f7b2f81634cf26fff1d4d03b3ec70b" kindref="member">loop()</ref> iteration. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Per call:<orderedlist>
<listitem><para>Forward up to CDC_TO_UART_BUDGET USB CDC bytes (Serial) to UART — DCS-BIOS stream to <ref refid="namespacePanelBridge" kindref="compound">PanelBridge</ref>.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Drain all UART bytes: 0xAA 0x55 + 4 bytes → parse controlId + value LE; dispatch to HID lists any other byte → append to the host-bound line; on <computeroutput>\n</computeroutput> the whole line is written to USB CDC, or dropped and counted (see below) 0xAA + non-0x55 → both bytes go to the line, which makes it corrupt; resume IDLE</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>If any HID setter fired, send the HID report exactly once.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Status LEDs, UART error counters, FAULT self-clear.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>USB recovery ladder (<ref refid="LinkRecovery_8h" kindref="compound">LinkRecovery.h</ref>).</para>
</listitem></orderedlist>
</para>
<para><bold>Never blocks on the host.</bold> A line is written only if the CDC FIFO has room for all of it; otherwise it is dropped whole — never truncated — and counted in GatewayDiag::linesDropped. A line holding anything but printable ASCII (0x20–0x7E) and its <computeroutput>\n</computeroutput> is dropped as corrupt, and one longer than RELAY_LINE_MAX as overlong. Everything <ref refid="namespacePanelBridge" kindref="compound">PanelBridge</ref> sends the host is a newline-framed DCS-BIOS message, so neither happens on a healthy link. Calibration frames are written whole or not at all in the same way.</para>
<para><simplesect kind="note"><para>The first call arms a WATCHDOG_MS hardware watchdog; after that, <ref refid="namespaceSimGateway_1aa8f7b2f81634cf26fff1d4d03b3ec70b" kindref="member">loop()</ref> must be called at least that often or the chip resets (production builds only).</para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="note"><para>Node-status reporting (#86) needs no handling here: <ref refid="namespacePanelBridge" kindref="compound">PanelBridge</ref>&apos;s <computeroutput>_NODE_STATUS</computeroutput> DCS-BIOS messages are ASCII (≤ 0x7F) forwarded by step 2, and the host&apos;s roster request is a DCS-BIOS export write (addr 0x86FE) forwarded by step 1. Both transit transparently.</para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="note"><para>Parser state persists across calls — frames split across iterations assemble correctly. </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
        </inbodydescription>
